Ladybird now hides a block-level replaced element that comes after a
line-clamp container’s clamp point, inside inline content, with the
rest of the content after the clamp point, as it already did for any
other block-level box there. Blink does the same: Its LineClampData::
IsHidden() hides each box that’s laid out once IsPastClampPoint() is
true, whatever kind of box it is.
